.TH "RAPTOR-EDIT" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor\-edit \- duplicate elements or copy a block's data
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor edit\fR [\-h] MODEL ACTION ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Structural edits shared with the canvas: duplicate a selection with fresh ids and names, or copy one block's data groups onto others. The model file changes only when the in\-place flag is given.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBduplicate\fR
copy elements with fresh ids
.TP
\fBpaste\-data\fR
Paste Special: copy data groups, tags or the comment onto elements
.TP
\fBout\-of\-service\fR
take blocks, events or hierarchies out of service
.SH RAPTOR EDIT DUPLICATE
\fBraptor edit duplicate\fR licate [\-h] [\-\-copies N] [\-\-dx T] [\-\-dy T] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}] ELEMENT [ELEMENT ...]
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-copies\fR \fIN\fR
how many copies (default 1)
.TP
\fB\-\-dx\fR \fIT\fR
each copy's offset to the right, in diagram units (default 40)
.TP
\fB\-\-dy\fR \fIT\fR
each copy's offset downward (default 40)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the result back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR EDIT PASTE\-DATA
\fBraptor edit paste\-data\fR e\-data [\-h] \-\-source ELEMENT \-\-targets NAMES [\-\-groups NAMES] [\-\-tag\-mode {add,replace}] [\-\-comment\-mode {replace,append,empty}] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}]
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fIELEMENT\fR
the element to copy from
.TP
\fB\-\-targets\fR \fINAMES\fR
comma list of elements (blocks, unless only Tags or Comment are pasted)
.TP
\fB\-\-groups\fR \fINAMES\fR
comma list (default Failure,Repair): Failure, Repair, Logistics delays, Repair crews, Spares, PM, Costs, Dependency, Phasing, Tags, Comment
.TP
\fB\-\-tag\-mode\fR \fI{add|replace}\fR
Tags: add to the targets' tags (default) or replace them
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\-mode\fR \fI{replace|append|empty}\fR
Comment: replace (default), append, or fill only where the target has none (empty)
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the result back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH RAPTOR EDIT OUT\-OF\-SERVICE
\fBraptor edit out\-of\-service\fR ervice [\-h] [\-\-state {cut,linked,in\-service}] [\-\-in\-place] [\-f {text,json}] [ELEMENT ...]
.PP
A what\-if switch that leaves the element's data alone: cut (down for the whole run), linked (never fails) or in\-service (back to normal). A hierarchy covers everything inside it. Saved in .rbds only.
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI{cut|linked|in\-service}\fR
cut (default), linked or in\-service
.TP
\fB\-\-in\-place\fR
write the result back to MODEL
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR \fI{text|json}\fR
output format (default text)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\fR(1)
